---
import '../../styles/global.css';
import AcademicsFooter from '../../components/AcademicsFooter.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<html lang='en'>
  <head>
    <meta charset='UTF-8' />
    <meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0' />
    <title>Terms of Attachment | SPMH Academics & Internships</title>
  </head>
  <body class='bg-slate-50 text-slate-900 antialiased'>
    <header
      class='sticky top-0 z-40 bg-white/95 backdrop-blur border-b border-slate-200'>
      <div
        class='max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 h-16 flex items-center justify-between'>
        <a
          href='/academics-and-partnerships'
          class='text-slate-500 hover:text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium flex items-center gap-1 transition-colors'>
          ← Back to Academics Hub
        </a>
        <span class='font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight text-xs sm:text-sm'
          >Terms of Attachment</span
        >
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class='max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20'>
      <div class='mb-10 space-y-2'>
        <h1
          class='text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight'>
          Terms of Attachment
        </h1>
        <p class='text-sm text-slate-500'>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        <p class='text-sm text-slate-600'>
          These terms govern clinical rotations, administrative attachments, and
          internships undertaken at St. Paul's Mission Hospital (SPMH) under the
          Academics & Internships program.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class='prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-10 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-700'>
        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>1. Eligibility</h2>
          <p>
            Applicants must be currently enrolled at a recognized academic
            institution and submit an attachment request through the official
            application form, sponsored or confirmed by their home institution
            where required.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            2. Application & Placement
          </h2>
          <ul class='list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5'>
            <li>
              Submitting an application does not guarantee placement.
              Attachments are subject to departmental capacity and HR approval.
            </li>
            <li>
              Proposed start and end dates are requests; SPMH will confirm final
              dates based on departmental scheduling.
            </li>
            <li>
              Applicants will receive a unique reference code to track their
              application status.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            3. Conduct & Professional Standards
          </h2>
          <p>
            Attachees are expected to adhere to SPMH's professional conduct
            standards, dress code, and departmental protocols at all times.
            Attachees must follow the direction of their assigned clinical or
            administrative preceptor and comply with all applicable hospital
            policies.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>4. Confidentiality</h2>
          <p>
            Attachees will have access to sensitive patient and institutional
            information in the course of their placement. Strict confidentiality
            must be maintained at all times, in line with applicable patient
            privacy and data protection obligations. Any breach of
            confidentiality may result in immediate termination of the
            attachment.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            5. Scope of Supervision
          </h2>
          <p>
            Clinical rotations are conducted under the direct supervision of
            certified SPMH clinical preceptors. Attachees may not perform any
            clinical procedure beyond their training level or without direct
            supervision.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>6. Liability</h2>
          <p>
            Attachees participate in the program at their own risk. SPMH expects
            sponsoring institutions to maintain appropriate student insurance
            coverage for the duration of the attachment period.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            7. Termination of Attachment
          </h2>
          <p>
            SPMH reserves the right to end an attachment early in cases of
            misconduct, breach of confidentiality, or failure to meet
            professional standards, with notice to the attachee's home
            institution where applicable.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>
            8. Institutional Partnerships
          </h2>
          <p>
            Partnership inquiries submitted by academic institutions are
            reviewed by SPMH Administration and may lead to a formal Memorandum
            of Understanding (MOU) governing the terms of an ongoing attachment
            pipeline.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class='space-y-3'>
          <h2 class='text-lg font-bold text-slate-900'>9. Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these terms should be directed to SPMH Human
            Resources at
            <a
              href='mailto:hr@spmh.co.ke'
              class='text-blue-600 font-semibold underline'>hr@spmh.co.ke</a
            >.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p class='text-xs text-slate-400 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200'>
          This is a general institutional template. It should be reviewed by a
          qualified legal professional before being treated as a binding
          agreement.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <AcademicsFooter />
  </body>
</html>
